# Credentials for the Node scripts only — `pnpm smoke:live`, `pnpm reconcile`
# and `pnpm symbols:generate`. No addon reads this file: each asks for its own
# credentials in its setup form and keeps them in Wealthfolio's keyring.
#
# Copy to `.env` (which git ignores) and fill that in. THIS file is tracked —
# it holds placeholders and nothing else. A real key committed here is the one
# mistake this repo has already made once; see CONTRIBUTING.md.

# ── Trading 212 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Settings → API in the mobile app. Read access is all that is needed.
T212_API_KEY=
T212_API_SECRET=

# ── Kraken ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kraken Pro → Settings → API → Add API key. Tick exactly three boxes:
#   Funds permissions  · Query                        (Balance)
#   Orders and trades  · Query closed orders & trades (TradesHistory)
#   Data               · Query ledger entries         (Ledgers)
#
# Those three see everything: deposits, withdrawals, trades and Earn rewards.
# The rest are write paths that add no read access, which is worth spelling out
# because it is not obvious from the checkbox names:
#   Earn        — gates Earn/Allocate and Earn/Deallocate ONLY, i.e. moving
#                 funds between strategies. Reading your allocations
#                 (Earn/Allocations) needs "Funds · Query", already ticked;
#                 reward history is in the ledger; staked balances show up in
#                 Balance as suffixed assets (XBT.S, ETH.F, DOT.M).
#   Withdraw    — gates the actual Withdraw call. Not needed for detail:
#                 WithdrawStatus accepts "Query ledger entries" instead.
#   Deposit     — gates DepositAddresses, which generates addresses.
#                 DepositStatus needs only "Funds · Query".
#   Export data — for Kraken's CSV export endpoints, which we do not use.
#   Query open orders & trades — unfilled orders; nothing to import.
#
# Leave all six toggles Off. "Query start date" and "Query end date" matter
# most: either one cuts off how far back the key can read, which silently
# truncates a backfill.
#
# KRAKEN_API_SECRET is Kraken's "Private key" — a base64 string, pasted
# verbatim. Do not decode it; the signing step base64-decodes it itself.
# Kraken shows it once, so copy it before closing the dialog.
#
# Use this key for nothing else: Kraken requires a strictly increasing nonce
# per key, so a second tool sharing it produces "Invalid nonce" errors that
# look exactly like a bug in this connector. If that happens anyway, turn on
# the key's Custom nonce window at 5000–10000.
KRAKEN_API_KEY=
KRAKEN_API_SECRET=
